HEOR Studio — licensing
=======================

This repository is split-licensed. Which license applies depends on which
package the code lives in.

  packages/core   AGPL-3.0-only   (see packages/core/LICENSE)
  packages/web    AGPL-3.0-only   (see packages/web/LICENSE)
  packages/mcp    Apache-2.0      (see packages/mcp/LICENSE)


Why the split
-------------

`core` holds the study-spec schema, the deterministic SAS/SQL emitters, and the
verification harness — the substance of the project. It is AGPL-3.0-only so that
improvements to the emitters stay available to the analysts who depend on them,
including when the software is offered over a network.

`mcp` is a thin protocol shim that exposes `core` to MCP hosts. It is Apache-2.0
so that hosts and clients can integrate without taking on copyleft obligations
for their own code.


IMPORTANT — what Apache-2.0 on `mcp` does and does not mean
-----------------------------------------------------------

The MCP server's own source is Apache-2.0. However, the published
`@heor-studio/mcp` artifact BUNDLES `@heor-studio/core` (see
packages/mcp/tsup.config.ts), and `core` is AGPL-3.0-only. The distributed
binary is therefore a combined work and is governed by the AGPL-3.0 terms.

In practice:

  * Reading, modifying, and re-licensing `packages/mcp` SOURCE — Apache-2.0.
  * Distributing or network-serving the BUILT MCP server — AGPL-3.0-only
    applies, because `core` is compiled into it.
  * Using either to generate study code — the OUTPUT is yours. Code generated
    from your own study specification is not a derivative work of this project,
    and nothing here places any license condition on your study, your results,
    or your data.

If that combination does not suit your deployment, run the MCP server against
`core` as a separate dependency rather than as a bundled build, or contact the
maintainer to discuss alternative terms.


